WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:05.580
David, why do you think Christian profits
are on the rise again?

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:07.200
This is a really interesting question.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:12.840
And there's a super compelling article in
The New York Times about Christian prophets

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:14.400
and their predictions.

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:21.570
And one of the points that the article makes
is that right now there is a real hunger for

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:28.700
reassurance and clarity in many areas of American
culture.

00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:35.350
In particular, we have seen Donald Trump be
the least popular president by approval rating

00:00:35.350 --> 00:00:37.260
in the polling era.

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:42.809
Leave the White House with the lowest approval
rating of any president in the polling era,

00:00:42.809 --> 00:00:47.670
with so many failed promises from Donald Trump.

00:00:47.670 --> 00:00:53.159
And for the left who never believed any of
that stuff to begin with and on average is

00:00:53.159 --> 00:00:54.999
less religious than the right.

00:00:54.999 --> 00:00:59.690
And to the extent that the left is religious,
it tends to be less the sort of charismatic

00:00:59.690 --> 00:01:05.160
evangelical Christianity that is so much more
prominent on the right in the United States.

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:11.030
The left isn't really looking for prophecy,
for reassurance and clarity, because much

00:01:11.030 --> 00:01:13.520
of the left never believe Trump to begin with.

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:21.750
And much of the left doesn't look to these
sort of televangelist equivalents for guidance

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:30.520
on the right, you saw an initially resistant
evangelical Christian wing of America resist

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:34.940
Trump at the beginning, sort of get behind
Ted Cruz and some other candidates in the

00:01:34.940 --> 00:01:36.880
2016 Republican primary.

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:41.010
Eventually, Trump won and they certainly weren't
going to vote for Hillary Clinton.

00:01:41.010 --> 00:01:45.860
So you saw a lot of these folks who would
not normally go for the multiple times divorced

00:01:45.860 --> 00:01:53.320
guy who pays off of porn stars and whatever
else, OK, they went with him and then everything

00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:54.590
he promised he didn't do.

00:01:54.590 --> 00:01:58.020
Now some of them just continue to insist he
did all of it.

00:01:58.020 --> 00:02:01.790
He was the most pro-life president in all
of this different stuff.

00:02:01.790 --> 00:02:06.340
But many of them now are seeking some kind
of reassurance and clarity after seeing Trump

00:02:06.340 --> 00:02:11.560
not do any of the stuff he promised to do
and then lose to Joe Biden, who, despite actually

00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:17.040
being more devoutly religious than Donald
Trump, is Catholic and is a Democrat, which

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:22.690
does not go too well for a lot of these charismatic
and evangelical Christian communities.

00:02:22.690 --> 00:02:29.350
So there's a big demand for someone who will
tell you in clear terms, here's what's going

00:02:29.350 --> 00:02:30.350
to happen.

00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:34.920
And that is part of the reason why Christian
prophets are sort of seeing this resuscitation.

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:41.430
The newly popular, once again, widely making
wrong predictions, as has always been the

00:02:41.430 --> 00:02:42.430
case.

00:02:42.430 --> 00:02:48.459
Now, interestingly, astrology is also expanding
in popularity and the number of Americans

00:02:48.459 --> 00:02:52.340
who believe in psychics are also expanding.

00:02:52.340 --> 00:03:00.370
And I think that this is just a general sort
of reaction to uncertain political times,

00:03:00.370 --> 00:03:05.600
combined with a global hundred year pandemic
and the desire to have someone who will tell

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:10.651
you, here's how things are going to be in
your life, in the political future of the

00:03:10.651 --> 00:03:13.020
United States, etc..

00:03:13.020 --> 00:03:18.349
We know that at minimum, one third of Americans
say that they're suffering from stress and

00:03:18.349 --> 00:03:21.400
anxiety as a result of the pandemic.

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:24.819
When we ask when will it be over, we don't
really know.

00:03:24.819 --> 00:03:29.150
We're starting to get more clarity, at least
on the trajectory over the next few months.

00:03:29.150 --> 00:03:31.849
And things are looking better and hopefully
it'll keep going that way.

00:03:31.849 --> 00:03:36.540
But for a year now, we've had such uncertainty
that it is natural that people would want

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:42.270
answers and they would want someone who will
tell you definitively who is more arrogant

00:03:42.270 --> 00:03:49.180
in their predictions than these particular
televangelist type Christian prophets whose

00:03:49.180 --> 00:03:50.180
income and.

00:03:50.180 --> 00:03:55.379
Livelihood depends on even if they don't know
what the hell's going to happen, telling you

00:03:55.379 --> 00:03:57.000
that they definitely do.

00:03:57.000 --> 00:04:03.300
And because of that, I'm not particularly
surprised that this world of Christian punditry

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:06.800
and prophecy has surged in popularity.

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:10.020
If I'm missing something in that analysis,
let me know.

00:04:10.020 --> 00:04:11.880
I'm curious to hear from you.

00:04:11.880 --> 00:04:15.120
We have a fantastic bonus show for you today.

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:20.840
Make sure you get instant access by becoming
a member at Join Pakman dot com.

